From 356e258e469497b89eaaaa969b56f3f456847f23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:23:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] Add LAN GAME menu, gamepad LAN setup screen, in-game
 record entry and top 10

- Main menu: LAN GAME in the 4th column (VS / Battle).
- LAN setup screen drawn with the game font, all controller-driven: host or
  join, your address / host address, name, players on this PC, input delay,
  port, games found on the network, who's in.
- Netplay protocol v2: several players per PC (8 in all), players numbered
  PC by PC, multi-pad input messages, per-PC hashes; UDP LAN discovery and a
  local address lookup.
- A LAN GAME runs like Couch Party in lockstep: every player's cursor on
  character select, VS/Battle race, results; each PC draws only its own
  players' views. Quitting ends the session for everyone.
- Time Trial name entry is drawn in the game (no window), gamepad only, with
  Z for the driver's name and START+B to skip.
- DATA screen: a TOP 10 page (player name, driver, time, best lap) when a
  track is opened; Z flips to the game's own records.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qq7B1uqfWVWykYRDDMiuXa
